<%# Server-rendered feed tabs: Everyone (global) | Following (signed-in only) |
    Discover (search, Phase 2.3). Not a client filter — plain links that reload the
    feed with ?filter= (Everyone/Following) or navigate to the search page (Discover).

    14px medium, hairline rule underneath, active tab indigo with a 2px indigo underline
    (docs/design-system/components/navigation/FeedTabs.prompt.md). That is what the markup
    below already spelled out, so the classes are unchanged.

    These stay anchors rather than `ds_button_classes`: FeedTabs.prompt.md calls them "real
    page-level scopes, not client filters", and the DS's own Button is a pill — its `link`
    variant hard-codes `p-0` (which fights the tab's `py-2`), `justify-center` and
    `active:scale-95`, and carries no underline, which IS the active state here. A helper
    that has to be overridden on every axis is not the helper for the job.

    Discover is a distinct controller (SearchController), not a `?filter=` value, so its
    "active" check is `controller_name == "search"` rather than reading `params[:filter]` —
    on the feed itself it is simply a link, never active.

    `aria-current` because the active scope is otherwise signalled by colour alone. %>
<% following = params[:filter] == "following" && user_signed_in? %>
<% discover = controller_name == "search" %>
<%# One string per state rather than two mirrored ternaries: the colour and the underline
    must never disagree about which scope is showing. %>
<% active = "py-2 no-underline text-primary border-b-2 border-primary" %>
<% idle = "py-2 no-underline text-grey" %>
<nav class="flex gap-4 border-b border-gray-100 mb-4 text-sm font-medium">
  <%= link_to "Everyone", root_path,
        class: (following || discover) ? idle : active,
        aria: {current: ("page" unless following || discover)} %>
  <% if user_signed_in? %>
    <%= link_to "Following", root_path(filter: "following"),
          class: following ? active : idle,
          aria: {current: ("page" if following)} %>
  <% end %>
  <%= link_to "Discover", search_path,
        class: discover ? active : idle,
        aria: {current: ("page" if discover)} %>
</nav>
